# Frame Budget

Every frame has a fixed budget (16.6 ms at 60 fps, shared with rendering). No system may do **unbounded** work in a single frame.

## No unbounded per-frame work

Work proportional to "all entities", "all files", "whole grid" must be bounded or amortized.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — O(n²) scan every frame
private void Update()
{
    foreach (var a in _units)
    {
        foreach (var b in _units)
        {
            CheckAggro(a, b);
        }
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — time-sliced: fixed number of checks per frame, round-robin cursor
private int _scanCursor;
private const int ChecksPerFrame = 32;

private void Update()
{
    for (int step = 0; step < ChecksPerFrame; step++)
    {
        _scanCursor = (_scanCursor + 1) % _units.Count;
        CheckAggroAround(_units[_scanCursor]);
    }
}
```

Amortization tools: round-robin cursors, work queues drained N-items-per-frame, coroutines yielding between chunks, dirty flags so only changed items are reprocessed.

## No per-frame scene walks

Never call these in `Update`/`FixedUpdate`/`LateUpdate` or per-message handlers:

- `GameObject.Find`, `FindObjectOfType` / `FindAnyObjectByType`, `FindObjectsByType`
- `GetComponentsInChildren` on large hierarchies
- `Resources.*`, asset loads

Resolve references once in `Awake`/`Start` (or via serialized fields) and cache them.

## Events over polling

If a value changes rarely, don't check it every frame — raise an event when it changes.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — polling a rarely changing value, plus per-frame string alloc
private void Update()
{
    _scoreLabel.text = $"Score: {_game.Score}";
}

// ✅ GOOD — update only on change
private void OnEnable()
{
    _game.ScoreChanged += OnScoreChanged;
}

private void OnScoreChanged(int score)
{
    _scoreLabel.text = $"Score: {score.ToString()}";
}
```

Polling is fine for genuinely continuous input (mouse position, axis values).

## Spread startup cost

Heavy initialization (pool pre-warm, grid building, deserialization) belongs in the loading phase — behind the loading screen — not lazily on first use mid-gameplay.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No new per-frame work proportional to total entity/asset count without slicing
- [ ] No Find/GetComponent/asset-load calls per frame; references cached
- [ ] Rarely changing values drive UI via events, not `Update` polling
- [ ] Heavy setup runs during loading, not on first use
